luating this identity at $t=0$ gives\n\n$$\nx(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)c,\n$$\n\nwhich is exactly line $\\text{L3}.$ Therefore, $\\text{L3}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ by $\\text{evaluating both sides at }t=0.$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L3}$, $\\text{L4},$ and $\\text{L5}.$ From $\\text{L3}$ we have\n\n$$\nx(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)c,\n$$\n\nand from $\\text{L4}$ we know ${Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}.$ Substituting ${Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}$ into $x(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)c$ gives\n\n$$\nx(0)={I}_{n}c=c,\n$$\n\nwhich is exactly line $\\text{L5}.$ Thus, $\\text{L5}$ follows from lines $\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}$ by $\\text{substituting }{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}\\text{ into }x(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)c.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L1}$, $\\text{L2},$ $\\text{L5},$ and $\\text{L6}.$ From $\\text{L1}$ we have ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At},$ and from $\\text{L5}$ we know $c=x(0).$ Substituting ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ from $\\text{L1}$ and $c=x(0)$ from $\\text{L5}$ into $x(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c$ (line $\\text{L2}$), we obtain\n\n$$\nx(t)={e}^{At}\\,x(0).\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L6}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ and substitution from $\\text{L1}\\text{ and }\\text{L5}.$" 13194139533470 17592186045585 true] [17592186396943 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396944 13194139533470 17592186045585 true] [17592186396943 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396945 13194139533470 17592186045585 true] [17592186396943 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396946 13194139533470 17592186045585 true] [17592186396943 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396947 13194139533470 17592186045585 true] [17592186396943 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 13194139533470 17592186045585 true] [17592186396943 1077 "field-3" 13194139533470 17592186045585 true] [17592186396943 1079 #edb/ref 17592186396945 13194139533470 17592186045585 true] [17592186396943 1080 #uuid "62e5d724-e4aa-50ec-8d98-2ca352e011f4" 13194139533470 17592186045585 true] [17592186396944 1081 "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}$" 13194139533470 17592186045585 true] [17592186396944 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533470 17592186045585 true] [17592186396944 1